  ],
  "text": "In the deep sea, glowing is not rare. It is the normal way to live. Sunlight gives up about two hundred metres down. Below that there is nothing. So most animals down there stopped waiting for light and started making it. Two chemicals, mixed together. That is the entire trick. Some use it as bait. A lamp on a stick, in permanent darkness. Some use it to disappear. They light their own belly to match the water above. And it did not evolve once. It evolved separately, dozens of times over. Which tells you how useful light becomes when there is none at all. So most living things on this planet are ones you will never see. And they are glowing. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
